{
 "_comment": "Curated description of every mirrored SDRBench dataset. 'archive' is relative to globus_base. 'rules' map file globs (matched against the file name or its path inside the variant) to a numpy dtype and a C-order shape (slowest dimension first, as in the SZ3 CI dataset table); shape \"1d\" means a flat array. Every non-text file must match a rule and its size must equal prod(shape)*itemsize, or the catalog build fails. A rule with dtype null marks a non-array file (HDF5, ADIOS .bp, ...). Variant keys are the folder names on Hugging Face; 'name' is the variant name used in the Python API (the first variant listed is the default).",
 "globus_base": "https://g-d0cd3f.fd635.8443.data.globus.org/raw-data/",
 "page": "https://sdrbench.github.io/datasets.html",
 "excluded": {
  "NSTX_GPI/nstx_data_ornl_demo.bp": "owner asks to be contacted before results are published; not redistributed",
  "brown_synth/SDRBENCH-BROWN-33554433.tar.gz": "not mirrored",
  "EXASKY/HACC/multi-timesteps/4507.tar.gz": "broken link on Globus (HTTP 404)"
 },
